{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>A sabbath to YHWH your Elohim.</b> And not to you — meaning: rest and cease from all labor and toil." "<b>You shall not do any work.</b> Any work whatsoever — like 'after any likeness' (Deut. 4:25), like 'any widow or orphan' (Exod. 22:21)." "<b>And your male slave and your female slave.</b> What it did not explain here — on account of what male slave and female slave rest — it went back and explained in Mishneh Torah, on account of 'you shall remember that you were a slave in the land of Egypt' like him, and He redeemed you."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "The comment cites two biblical phrases where כל precedes a noun with no limiting sense, to show כל מלאכה likewise means 'any work whatsoever.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:02.297037939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}